  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I noticed in the recent update, that my IPD scale is off.\n\nI have my SteamVR to always display a square with an arrow to show direction, which also lets me see where my RL floor is.  \n\nI have had the issue of IPD scaling being off with my avatars, but I had a work around where I'd set Stand height to my Real height, change to seated mode, and then adjust the height down to 4'10\" (depending on the avatar, but this case, my fox avatar)  and that would keep RL floor aligned with VRchat's floors.\n\nIn the update, I noticed a few things:\n\n1. I have to change the height to 4'3\" now, because the VRchat floor appears further down that it used to.\n\n2. On my other avatar, changing to Seated mode, It no longer keeps the height set for my Standing mode height, and in fact sets me up even higher than I was in standing mode, making my legs stretched out fully (which they are digitigrade, so it looks wrong)  and I can no longer use that technique for my Phoenix avatar.\n\nthis is one of the reasons why I suggested a new way of doing IPD scaling (but it seems not many others care about it)",
